  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 24d0b860ee; owner-requested re-check of the 51 open P2 violated/todo_hard/todo_soft items; fixtures and outputs under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p2_review_11012026/C1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. repo_tier_offer.py:168-170 `interactive = sys.stdin.isatty(); if not interactive: return False` has been there since the feature's first commit (4b5478145d), so question (2) is answered: a non-TTY run never asks (verified: XDG_STATE_HOME=<empty> hypergumbo survey fx </dev/null -> rc 0, no prompt, no offers.json); under a PTY the prompt fires and 'n' records {repo_tier_examples: {accepted: false}}. 53ae8f9e01 (10-25, INV-kuroj) added the overlap guard: should_offer(analysed=~/hypergumbo) -> False, so the filed repro (`hypergumbo hypergumbo`) no longer fires; analysed=<other repo> or None -> True. Call site cli.py:13926 in main()'s generic post-command hook. Residual: the first interactive analysis of any OTHER repo on a box with ~/hypergumbo and no recorded decision still prompts once, at the end of a possibly long run. Title re-scoped. ROOT CAUSE: an offer wired into main()'s post-command hook, gated on environment rather than on the command or a flag (singleton). Status unchanged."  # 2b38
